  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday) \nIssued at 806 PM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nA continued warming trend is expected during the long term forecast\nperiod as the upper level pattern shows a trough over the West Coast\nwith ridging over the Central and Eastern US. On Thursday, sfc high\npressure over the Carolinas will bring dry and mild weather to the\nTennessee Valley. By Friday, a low pressure system is then forecast \nto develop off the east coast of FL and move to the north and east. \nThere is some uncertainty on if this wave will move onshore, which \nmay bring a very low chance of precip to our eastern areas on Sunday.\nHowever, the model blends seem to keep this away with the \naforementioned sfc high pressure remaining entrenched to our north \nand east. Therefore, a dry forecast continues through the end of the \nweekend with afternoon highs each afternoon rising into the lower 70s\nand overnight lows in the upper 30s to lower 40s.",
